ARTICLE 6 — ENFORCEMENT AND REMEDIES
===============================================================================

6.1 Right to Issue Cease-and-Desist and Lawyer's Letters. The Licensor
    expressly reserves the right, in its sole discretion, to issue
    cease-and-desist letters, lawyer's letters (律师函), formal legal
    notices, and other written demands to any person or entity that the
    Licensor reasonably believes is using, distributing, or exploiting the
    Software or any Derivative Work in violation of this License, including
    without limitation any unauthorized Commercial Use. The issuance of such a
    letter or notice does not waive any right or remedy available to the
    Licensor at law or in equity.

6.2 Injunctive Relief. You acknowledge that any breach or threatened breach of
    this License, including any unauthorized Commercial Use, may cause
    irreparable harm to the Licensor for which monetary damages may be an
    inadequate remedy. Accordingly, the Licensor shall be entitled to seek
    injunctive relief, specific performance, and other equitable remedies (in
    addition to any other remedies available at law) in any court of competent
    jurisdiction, without the requirement to post a bond or prove actual
    damages.

6.3 Damages and Account of Profits. In the event of any breach of this
    License, the Licensor shall be entitled to recover from the breaching
    party:
    (a) all actual damages suffered by the Licensor as a result of the breach;
    (b) an account of all profits, revenues, or other benefits derived by the
        breaching party from the unauthorized use, distribution, or
        exploitation of the Software or any Derivative Work;
    (c) statutory damages, where available under applicable law;
    (d) punitive or exemplary damages, where permitted by applicable law, in
        cases of willful or egregious breach.

6.4 Limited Cure Period. In the case of a non-commercial, unintentional, and
    non-willful breach of this License (excluding any unauthorized Commercial
    Use, which is not subject to cure), the breaching party may cure such
    breach within thirty (30) days of receiving written notice from the
    Licensor. If the breach is cured within such period, the Licensor may, in
    its sole discretion, elect not to pursue further remedies for that
    specific breach. This cure right does not apply to:
    (a) any unauthorized Commercial Use;
    (b) any willful or repeated breach;
    (c) any breach that causes material harm to the Licensor or any third
        party;
    (d) any breach of Article 5 (Commercial Use Authorization) or Article 6
        (Enforcement and Remedies).

6.5 Audit Rights. If you hold a valid Commercial Authorization, the Licensor
    shall have the right, upon reasonable prior written notice (not less than
    ten (10) business days), to audit or cause an independent third party to
    audit your use of the Software and its Derivative Works, solely to verify
    compliance with the terms of the Commercial Authorization and this
    License. Such audit shall be conducted during normal business hours and in
    a manner that minimizes disruption to your operations. If the audit
    reveals material non-compliance, you shall bear the reasonable costs of
    the audit in addition to any other remedies available to the Licensor.

6.6 Costs and Attorneys' Fees. In any legal action or proceeding arising out
    of or relating to this License, the prevailing party shall be entitled to
    recover its reasonable costs, expenses, and attorneys' fees (including
    fees incurred in connection with the issuance of cease-and-desist or
    lawyer's letters) from the non-prevailing party, in addition to any other
    relief granted.

6.7 Reservation of Rights. The remedies set forth in this Article 6 are
    cumulative and not exclusive. The Licensor reserves all rights and
    remedies available at law, in equity, under statute, or otherwise,
    including but not limited to claims for copyright infringement, patent
    infringement, trademark infringement, breach of contract, and unfair
    competition. Nothing in this License shall be construed as limiting the
    Licensor's right to pursue any or all such remedies concurrently or
    sequentially.

