ARTICLE 10 — TERMINATION
===============================================================================

10.1 Automatic Termination for Breach. If you breach any term or condition of
     this License, all rights and licenses granted to you under this License
     (including the copyright license under Article 2 and the patent license
     under Article 3) shall terminate automatically and immediately, without
     the need for any notice from the Licensor, unless the breach is a
     non-commercial, unintentional, and curable breach as described in
     Section 6.4 and is cured within the applicable cure period.

10.2 Effect of Termination. Upon termination of this License for any reason:
     (a) you must immediately cease all use, reproduction, modification, and
         distribution of the Software and all Derivative Works;
     (b) you must destroy or permanently delete all copies of the Software and
         all Derivative Works in your possession, custody, or control, and
         certify such destruction in writing upon request by the Licensor;
     (c) any sublicenses previously granted by you to third parties shall
         terminate, except that copies lawfully distributed to third parties
         prior to termination may continue to be used by such third parties
         solely to the extent such third parties remain in compliance with this
         License.

10.3 Survival. The following provisions shall survive termination of this
     License: Article 1 (Definitions), Article 6 (Enforcement and Remedies),
     Article 7 (Trademarks), Article 8 (Disclaimer of Warranty), Article 9
     (Limitation of Liability), Article 10 (Termination), and Article 11
     (General Provisions), together with any other provisions that by their
     nature are intended to survive termination.

10.4 No Waiver by Termination. Termination of this License shall not affect
     any right or remedy of the Licensor that has accrued prior to or as a
     result of such termination, including the right to seek damages,
     injunctive relief, or any other remedy for any breach that occurred prior
     to termination.

